Trust the system CA store (/etc/ssl/certs, from ca-certificates) INSTEAD of the
roots compiled into bun, so a CA removed from ca-certificates (CVE-2026-111943,
eMudhra) stops being trusted without a bun rebuild. gominimal/pkgmgr-rs#1026.

Ported from the bun-v1.3.14 patch to bun-v1.4.4 (the Rust rewrite: the CLI
flags moved from src/cli/Arguments.zig to src/bun_core/Global.rs, and the
compiled-in roots became a lazy cert set). Same behaviour.

At bun-v1.4.4 there is still no upstream switch that does this:
  - us_get_default_ca_store() (packages/bun-usockets/src/crypto/root_certs.cpp)
    ALWAYS adds the compiled-in roots. --use-system-ca / NODE_USE_SYSTEM_CA=1
    only add the system roots to them (a union), so a distrust never applies.
  - --use-openssl-ca is parsed (Global.rs set_ca_store_from_flags) and then
    ignored: only --use-system-ca is stored. Upstream fixed that in
    oven-sh/bun#46542 (b70684d7, merged 2026-10-23), after bun-v1.4.4.

This patch:
  - Global.rs: a new exported Bun__Node__MinimalCAStore records which of
    --use-system-ca (0, also the default), --use-openssl-ca (1) or
    --use-bundled-ca (2) was passed. Commands that never parse those flags
    keep the default (0).
  - root_certs.cpp: the default store gets the system roots and OpenSSL's
    default paths, and the compiled-in roots only when (a) --use-bundled-ca, or
    (b) NODE_USE_SYSTEM_CA is 0/false/no/off (the opt-out), or (c) the system
    store is empty (no ca-certificates), so bun keeps working rather than trust
    nothing. (a) and (b) are upstream's store exactly, where --use-system-ca /
    NODE_USE_SYSTEM_CA=1 still add the system roots. --use-openssl-ca leaves
    the compiled-in roots and the system loader out, as #46542 does, even
    with the NODE_USE_SYSTEM_CA opt-out set (the explicit flag wins).
  - root_certs.cpp, OpenSSL default file: upstream drops each certificate
    the compiled-in set holds byte-for-byte, because upstream always adds
    that set. Here it is dropped only when the compiled-in set is added
    (upstream's store); otherwise the file keeps it. Without this,
    --use-openssl-ca (no system loader, no compiled-in roots) trusted only
    the roots bun does not compile in, i.e. almost none.

Not changed: tls.rootCertificates and tls.getCACertificates('bundled') still
list the compiled-in roots; tls.getCACertificates('default') (src/js/node/tls.ts)
is computed in JS and still lists them too. Connections use the native store.
NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS is still added. Drop this patch once bun's own default
replaces the bundled store, or move to --use-openssl-ca on a release that
carries #46542.

